From 745db3022f5384df63f0c2d494f76ef6dfd2936a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saikrishna Edupuganti <6157640+krsna1729@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:41:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fib: fix error code propagation on next hop update

When updating the next hop of an existing prefix, dir24_8_modify()
ignored the return value of modify_fib() and always returned 0. The
update can fail with -ENOSPC: a range it installs may need a new tbl8
group, for example in a /24 whose group was merged back into tbl24
because a more specific route there had the same next hop, and
install_to_fib() wants two free groups for such a range. With
10.0.0.0/23 -> 1, 10.0.0.0/25 -> 1 and only one free group, re-pointing
the /23 to 3 changed nothing, the RIB kept next hop 1, and the caller
was told it succeeded. Return the actual result, as commit 3aca5f52b5
did for trie_modify().

Fixes: 7dc7868b200d ("fib: add DIR24-8 dataplane algorithm")
Cc: stable@dpdk.org

Upstream-Status: Pending
BESS-Decision: D-132
---
 lib/fib/dir24_8.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/fib/dir24_8.c b/lib/fib/dir24_8.c
index 4c356b0..2aa2b05 100644
--- a/lib/fib/dir24_8.c
+++ b/lib/fib/dir24_8.c
@@ -503,7 +503,8 @@ dir24_8_modify(struct rte_fib *fib, uint32_t ip, uint8_t depth,
 			ret = modify_fib(dp, rib, ip, depth, next_hop);
 			if (ret == 0)
 				rte_rib_set_nh(node, next_hop);
-			return 0;
+
+			return ret;
 		}
 		if (depth > 24) {
 			tmp = rte_rib_get_nxt(rib, ip, 24, NULL,
-- 
